<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-paulistorum-turing-wavelength-s0-specimen-match> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila paulistorum Schnakenberg ocellar stripe at 2.4 µm (Pass 2) — Morphological realism / specimen match: 84/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The comparison figure shows the Haars male beside the 2.417 µm activator stripes and a basic-look frame in which those stripes are impressed on the photograph at α=0.18. Last-frame CV similarity is 85.9 (12-bin orientation, 24-bin radial FFT, structure-tensor coherency, occupancy) on a 640×480, 12-frame GIF. The score stays below 90 because the raw field is a subcellular stripe lattice, not a second photograph of the fly, and no ocellar TEM of this species is in the dataset." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
