    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-paulistorum-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila paulistorum Schnakenberg ocellar stripe at 2.4 µm (Pass 2) (Drosophila paulistorum)",
        "Drosophila paulistorum Schnakenberg ocellar stripe at 2.4 µm (Pass 2) faithfully reproduces Drosophila paulistorum morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-paulistorum-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-paulistorum-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-paulistorum-turing-wavelength-s0-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-paulistorum-turing-wavelength-s0-4> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-paulistorum-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Drosophila paulistorum specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-paulistorum-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Drosophila paulistorum" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: A signed nanopublication. No local nanopub profile was present.",
        "does_not_claim: That Dobzhansky & Spassky measured a 2.4 µm Turing wavelength.",
        "does_not_claim: That the catalog order orena → paulistorum → persimilis is a fossil lineage.",
        "does_not_claim: That the low-amplitude stripe impress on the habitus is an electron micrograph of ommochrome granules.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Diffusivity magnitude 0.478965 chosen so the maximum of σ(k), not only the determinant stationary point, equals 2.417 µm.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Nine-point Du sweep and equal-diffusion ablation on a periodic intra-ocellar patch.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Packing counts against the catalog neighbors D. orena and D. persimilis.",
        "reported_in_source: Dobzhansky & Spassky 1959: D. paulistorum is a willistoni-group cluster of incipient semispecies. Holocene, 0 Ma.",
        "reported_in_source: Haars 2018: the CC BY-SA 4.0 adult male photograph used as the habitus.",
        "reported_in_source: Schnakenberg 1979: the activator-inhibitor kinetics.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952 and Maini, Painter & Chau 1997: finite-k instability conditions (trace, determinant, diffusivity ratio).",
        "transfer_boundary: Gompel et al. 2005 is a wing-pigment citation only.",
        "transfer_boundary: The 2.417 µm length is the assigned subcellular rung, on the order of a Drosophila rhabdomere diameter. It is not a published paulistorum morphometric." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Drosophila paulistorum (Amazonian Incipient Semispecies Ring Complex Fly)" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "II. Anaima (Invertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Entoma (Arthropoda)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Drosophila" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-paulistorum-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/drosophila_paulistorum_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Drosophila paulistorum; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Dobzhansky & Spassky 1959: D. paulistorum is a willistoni-group cluster of incipient semispecies. Holocene, 0 Ma. | Turing 1952 and Maini, Painter & Chau 1997: finite-k instability conditions (trace, determinant, diffusivity ratio). | Schnakenberg 1979: the activator-inhibitor kinetics. | Haars 2018: the CC BY-SA 4.0 adult male photograph used as the habitus.; reconstructed_in_script: Diffusivity magnitude 0.478965 chosen so the maximum of σ(k), not only the determinant stationary point, equals 2.417 µm. | Nine-point Du sweep and equal-diffusion ablation on a periodic intra-ocellar patch. | Packing counts against the catalog neighbors D. orena and D. persimilis.; transfer_boundary: The 2.417 µm length is the assigned subcellular rung, on the order of a Drosophila rhabdomere diameter. It is not a published paulistorum morphometric. | Gompel et al. 2005 is a wing-pigment citation only.; does_not_claim: That Dobzhansky & Spassky measured a 2.4 µm Turing wavelength. | That the catalog order orena → paulistorum → persimilis is a fossil lineage. | That the low-amplitude stripe impress on the habitus is an electron micrograph of ommochrome granules. | A signed nanopublication. No local nanopub profile was present.]; other sources: Drosophila paulistorum male <https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Drosophila_paulistorum_male.png>; phenomenon_size: 1.9 µm (1.919e-06 m, log10=-5.717 m, tier=3_subcellular_um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 1.9 µm to 4.3 mm): 1.9 µm:drosophila-affinis-bioelectric-polarity, 6.0 µm:drosophila-affinis-vertex-packing, 96 µm:drosophila-affinis-turing-wavelength, 192 µm:drosophila-affinis-clock-wavefront, 432 µm:drosophila-affinis-morphogen-condensation, 528 µm:drosophila-affinis-elastic-buckling, 600 µm:drosophila-affinis-flux-canalization, 840 µm:drosophila-affinis-branching-tree" ;
